OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769457313
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, British and Irish diplomats have been
OL,6, trying to check reports that an Irish
OL,7, hostage in Lebanon is to be freed soon.
OL,9,FMr Brian Keenan was seized in April
OL,10,F1986 and although reports of his
OL,11,Fimminent release are being treated
OL,12,Fwith caution, they are seen as strong
OL,13,Fenough to investigate.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FThe Foreign Office in London says it
OL,16,Ftreating the matter seriously and the
OL,17,FIrish ambassador to the Middle East is
OL,18,Fgoing to Beirut.
OL,20,FThere are also rumours of the release
OL,21,Fsoon of Mr John McCarthy, a Briton.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-01-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49605
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769457313
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, An independent report into Thames TV's
OL,6, Death On The Rock documentary has
OL,7, cleared the programme of bias.
OL,9,FThe report by Lord Windlesham concluded
OL,10,Fthat there was no serious risk of
OL,11,Fprejudicing the inquest into the deaths
OL,12,Fof three IRA members in Gibraltar.
OL,14,FIt said there had been some mistakes in
OL,15,Fthe programme but it was an impartial
OL,16,Fpiece of journalism.
OL,18,FThe Government said it did not agree
OL,19,Fwith the main findings of the report,
OL,20,Fsaying the programme contained many
OL,21,Fserious and damaging inaccuracies.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-01-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49606
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769457313
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, The inquiry into Death on the Rock
OL,6, clears the programme makers of
OL,7, criticism on all but two points.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FThe programme's commentary and the
OL,10,Fhandling of one of the witnesses were
OL,11,Fconsidered by the report to be flawed.
OL,12,F
OL,13,F"The programme makers were experienced,
OL,14,Fpainstaking and persistent. They did
OL,15,Fnot bribe, bully or misrepresent those
OL,16,Fwho took part," the report said.
OL,17,F
OL,18,F"The programme was trenchant and
OL,19,Favoided triviality. Those who made it
OL,20,Fwere acting in good faith and without
OL,21,Fulterior motives."
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-01-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49607
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769457313
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Government says it "profoundly
OL,6, disagrees" with the main findings of a
OL,7, report which clears the TV programme
OL,8, Death on the Rock of biasC(104/204).
OL,10,FA joint statement by the Foreign Office
OL,11,Fand the Ministry of Defence said the
OL,12,Fprogramme contained many serious and
OL,13,Fdamaging inaccuracies.
OL,15,FIn a number of important particulars
OL,16,Fthe programme makers failed to pursue
OL,17,Fthe truth to clarify the facts or to
OL,18,Fpresent evidence impartially, the
OL,19,Fstatement said.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-01-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49608
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769457313
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G8/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Independent Broadcasting Authority
OL,6, is to clarify its guidelines on TV
OL,7, coverage of Northern Ireland terrorism
OL,8, after the Gibraltar reportC(104/204).
OL,10,FA spokesman for the IBA said the
OL,11,Fsuggestion in the report that the
OL,12,Fpresentation of the guidelines should
OL,13,Fbe revised was accepted.
OL,15,FLabour leader Mr Neil Kinnock said the
OL,16,Freport was "a devastating rebuttal" of
OL,17,Fthe Government's stand on the case.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FThe producer of Death on the Rock,
OL,20,FMr Roger Bolton, said the report was
OL,21,F"a complete vindication".
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-01-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49609
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769457313
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G9/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, About #3.5 billion needs to be spent on
OL,6, new and improved rail services to ease
OL,7, the problem of packed commuter trains
OL,8, around London, a study suggests.
OL,10,FThe central London rail study calls for
OL,11,Fthe creation of two new rail lines and
OL,12,Fmajor upgrading of existing services.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FTransport Secretary Paul Channon said
OL,15,Fmoney for the scheme would come from
OL,16,Fpassengers in the capital, not from
OL,17,Ftaxpayers in other regions.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FOther finance could come from property
OL,20,Fowners, developers and possibly grants,
OL,21,Fhe said.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-01-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49610
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769457313
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G10/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The NUT has expressed concern over the
OL,6, criticism of teachers involved in the
OL,7, school holiday in Austria last year
OL,8, when four Berkshire schoolboys died.
OL,10,FA spokesman for the teachers' union
OL,11,Fsaid he believed the teachers had acted
OL,12,Fin a professional and dedicated manner.
OL,14,FAn independent inquiry said teachers
OL,15,Ffrom Altwood School in Maidenhead may
OL,16,Fhave become complacent and should not
OL,17,Fhave allowed the boys to play alone.
OL,19,FThe four boys, aged between 13-15, fell
OL,20,Fover a precipice after wandering away
OL,21,Ffrom pupils left to play unsupervised.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-01-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49611
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769457313
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G11/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, An independent inquiry into the deaths
OL,6, of four Berkshire schoolboys, who died
OL,7, in a mountain fall, has called for
OL,8, tighter regulation of school trips.
OL,10,FThe report says there should be clearer
OL,11,Fplanning of holidays before they begin,
OL,12,Fmore information for parents and better
OL,13,Fbriefing of teachers over supervising.
OL,15,FIt criticised the "nature, form and
OL,16,Fcontent" of the trip to Austria and
OL,17,Fquestioned its educational significance
OL,19,FThe four boys were among a party of 45
OL,20,Fchildren from Altwood Church of England
OL,21,FSchool in Maidenhead, Berkshire.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-01-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49612
SC,0012
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769457313
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G12/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Government has given its approval
OL,6, for a new system of portable telephones
OL,7, which could cost as little as #50.
OL,9,FThe Secretary for Trade and Industry,
OL,10,FLord Young, said four contractors would
OL,11,Fbe allowed to operate a new Telepoint
OL,12,Fsystem.
OL,14,FCallers with portable telephones can
OL,15,Fdial numbers if they are standing
OL,16,Fwithin 100 yards of a Telepoint, an
OL,17,Felectronic mechanism to be installed at
OL,18,Fpoints around cities.
OL,20,FThe first contractor hopes to be
OL,21,Foperating by the end of the year.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-01-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49613
SC,0013
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769457313
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G13/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, More police officers are to patrol
OL,6, London's Underground, the transport
OL,7, minister Mr Michael Portillo has said.
OL,9,FMr Portillo said 80 more officers would
OL,10,Fbe allocated temporarily to the network
OL,11,Fand the British transport police would
OL,12,Fbe urged to recruit special constables.
OL,14,FThe move follows Government concern
OL,15,Fover the arrival in Britain of the New
OL,16,FYork "Guardian Angels" vigilante group.
OL,18,FThe vigilantes have begun training 60
OL,19,FLondon recruits to fight crime on the
OL,20,Funderground. The Lords is debating the
OL,21,Funderground's rising crime today.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-01-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49614
SC,0014
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769457313
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G14/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4 BACKGROUND
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##! ##########
OL,5, Four members of the New York vigilante
OL,6, group, the "Guardian Angels" arrived in
OL,7, Britain on Tuesday.
OL,9,FThey are training 60 London recruits,
OL,10,Fwho they expect to be operating as
OL,11,Fvigilantes in the capital by April.
OL,13,FPublic concern over safety on London's
OL,14,Funderground network has grown following
OL,15,Fthree murders last month.
OL,17,FThe latest crime figures show a rise in
OL,18,Fthe number of reported robberies in the
OL,19,Ffirst 11 months of 1988 to 1,143,
OL,20,Fcompared to 828 in 1987. But total
OL,21,Fcrimes fell by 1,000 to about 15,000.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-01-89 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49615
SC,0015
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1769457313
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0     G15/26
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, An Italian court has ruled that Roberto
OL,6, Calvi, the banker found dead hanging
OL,7, from London's Blackfriars Bridge seven
OL,8, years ago, was murdered.
OL,10,FThe ruling, by a civil court in Milan,
OL,11,Fenables Calvi's widow, Clara, to claim
OL,12,Fa #2 million life insurance policy.
OL,14,FMr Calvi was found hanging from the
OL,15,Fbridge with a noose around his head and
OL,16,Fheavy weights in his pocket.
OL,18,FA London coroner first gave a verdict
OL,19,Fof suicide. Police in London today
OL,20,Fsaid they would ask for an urgent
OL,21,Freport from Italy on the new ruling.
OL,23,T]CFrom 26-01-89 / teletextarchive.com
